const questions=[
{key:'delivery',group:'Software architecture',label:'How is the software supplied?',hint:'Use the product documentation. For a new solution, use the intended architecture. This identifies compatible service models only. Placement also requires confirmed location constraints, cloud permission and capacity or cost evidence.',options:[['saas','SaaS only — vendor-hosted solution'],['package','Installable software — servers / virtual machines'],['container','Containerized solution'],['modern','Custom solution compatible with managed runtimes'],['ai','Specialized AI workload — dedicated accelerator / model infrastructure'],['unknown','Not yet confirmed']]},
{key:'local',group:'Control & sovereignty',label:'Must the solution execute on institution-controlled premises?',hint:'Answer Yes only for an approved requirement covering execution or infrastructure control. Sensitive data alone does not automatically require local execution.',options:[['yes','Yes — mandatory local execution'],['no','No mandatory local execution requirement'],['unknown','To confirm with architecture / risk']]},
{key:'cloud',group:'Control & sovereignty',label:'Can external cloud processing and administration be permitted?',hint:'Consider data, backups, telemetry, jurisdiction, privileged access and encryption keys. This is institutional permission, not proof that a specific provider complies.',options:[['yes','Permitted, subject to provider and control validation'],['no','Prohibited for this solution'],['unknown','Not yet approved / unknown']]},
{key:'hybrid',group:'Dependencies & performance',label:'Does the service require components in both local and cloud environments?',hint:'Choose Yes for an intentional split architecture. A cloud solution calling local identity alone does not necessarily require composite placement.',options:[['yes','Yes — intentional local and cloud components'],['no','No — a single execution environment is suitable'],['unknown','Architecture boundary not yet defined']]},
{key:'proximity',group:'Dependencies & performance',label:'Is there a hard local proximity constraint?',hint:'Examples include latency that remote execution cannot meet, very high local data volumes, or direct connection to local dedicated equipment. Record measurements in the solution profile.',options:[['hard','Yes — remote execution cannot satisfy it'],['flexible','No — engineered remote connectivity is feasible'],['unknown','Needs measurement / confirmation']]},
{key:'hardware',group:'Software architecture',label:'Is local dedicated hardware required?',hint:'Examples: a locally controlled HSM, physical licensing device or specialized appliance. An available cloud GPU is not a local-only requirement.',options:[['local','Yes — local physical / dedicated equipment is mandatory'],['standard','No — standard or provider-supplied infrastructure is suitable'],['unknown','Software / hardware requirements not confirmed']]},
{key:'platform',group:'Software architecture',label:'Which hosting pattern is supported?',hint:'Select a supported pattern, not an aspiration. Confirm vendor support, runtime compatibility and licensing before finalizing.',options:[['managed','Managed runtime / database / platform services supported'],['self','Institution controls OS / middleware / virtual machines'],['private','Private cloud self-service platform supported'],['unknown','Not confirmed / not applicable to SaaS']]},
{key:'demand',group:'Economics & capacity',label:'What is the demand profile?',hint:'Consider peaks, idle periods, expected growth and time to provision. Elastic demand is a reason to consider cloud, not permission to bypass controls.',options:[['elastic','Variable / burst demand; rapid scaling needed'],['steady','Predictable, stable capacity'],['unknown','Sizing not yet established']]},
{key:'economics',group:'Economics & capacity',label:'What is the assessor’s lifecycle-economic conclusion?',hint:'Record an assessor-supplied conclusion requiring supporting evidence. Compare equivalent service requirements over the same assessment period, including operations, connectivity, security, recovery and exit. The tool does not calculate TCO or establish economic superiority. Leave unconfirmed if no comparable estimates exist.',options:[['cloud','Assessor conclusion — cloud favored; supporting evidence required'],['local','Assessor conclusion — local favored; supporting evidence required'],['similar','Assessor conclusion — comparable / no clear cost advantage'],['unknown','No comparable lifecycle cost evidence']]},
{key:'criticality',group:'Resilience & assurance',label:'What is the solution’s service criticality?',hint:'Use business impact and institutional tiers. High criticality strengthens recovery and assurance requirements; it does not automatically dictate placement.',options:[['high','High — critical institutional / mission impact'],['medium','Medium — significant but tolerable disruption'],['low','Low — limited impact and workable alternative'],['unknown','Business impact not yet assessed']]},
{key:'recovery',group:'Resilience & assurance',label:'Are recovery targets and dependencies defined?',hint:'Define RTO (restoration time in hours), RPO (acceptable data-loss window in minutes), backup independence, trusted recovery and the recovery order of dependencies. A target is not evidence of a tested design.',options:[['yes','Targets and recovery dependencies are documented'],['no','Not yet documented'],['unknown','Needs continuity review']]},
{key:'control',group:'Operating capability',label:'How much direct institutional operational control is required?',hint:'Separate accountable ownership from executing tasks. The institution retains accountability under every operating model.',options:[['retain','Institution must execute privileged / critical operations'],['shared','Institution and provider may divide operations'],['delegate','Operational execution may be delegated'],['unknown','Responsibility boundary not agreed']]},
{key:'skills',group:'Operating capability',label:'What internal operating capability is available?',hint:'Consider coverage, skills, on-call capacity, platform lifecycle, incident handling and recovery—not only project implementation skills.',options:[['strong','Internal team can operate the full scope'],['partial','Internal capability covers part of the scope'],['limited','Limited internal capability for this scope'],['unknown','Capability / coverage not assessed']]},
{key:'sourcing',group:'Operating capability',label:'Is external operational sourcing permitted?',hint:'Distinguish broad managed operations from bounded specialist support. Procurement permission does not establish supplier assurance.',options:[['yes','Broad managed operations permitted'],['specialist','Only bounded specialist support permitted'],['no','No external operational sourcing permitted'],['unknown','Sourcing policy / approval not confirmed']]},
{key:'networkExposure',group:'Infrastructure security',label:'Who needs network access to the solution?',hint:'Describe the required exposure, not whether a firewall is already installed. Consider users, APIs, integrations and administrative interfaces. Internet access does not require cloud hosting; internal access does not establish security.',options:[['internal','Institutional networks only'],['partners','Institutional networks and approved external partners'],['internet','Internet-facing users or APIs'],['mixed','Mixed internal, partner and internet-facing access'],['unknown','Access paths not yet defined']]},
{key:'securityIsolation',group:'Infrastructure security',label:'What isolation does the hosting environment require?',hint:'Record the required separation between workloads and administration. Dedicated infrastructure may exist locally or with a provider; validate the actual architecture rather than assuming that a location guarantees isolation.',options:[['baseline','Shared platform with standard access and network controls'],['segmented','Strong logical segmentation and separate administrative boundaries'],['dedicated','Dedicated physical resources / hardware isolation required'],['unknown','Isolation requirements not yet defined']]},
{key:'keyCustody',group:'Infrastructure security',label:'Who must control encryption keys and their lifecycle?',hint:'Include generation, access, rotation, revocation and recovery. Institution-controlled keys do not by themselves remove provider jurisdiction or administrative exposure.',options:[['institution','Institution retains control of keys and lifecycle decisions'],['shared','Institution and provider share responsibilities'],['provider','Provider-managed keys may be accepted subject to institutional review'],['unknown','Key ownership and recovery responsibilities not yet defined']]},
{key:'trustedRecovery',group:'Infrastructure security',label:'What recovery capability is required after a cyber compromise?',hint:'Cyber recovery concerns trustworthy backups, identities, configurations and administration after compromise. Backup or replication alone does not demonstrate that capability. Specify the requirement; evidence is reviewed outside this questionnaire.',options:[['isolated','Isolated / immutable recovery sources with separate administration'],['rebuild','Rebuild from trusted configurations, identities and protected data sources'],['both','Isolated recovery sources and trusted rebuild capability'],['undefined','Only ordinary backup / DR is described; cyber recovery still needs definition'],['unknown','Cyber-recovery requirements not yet assessed']]},
{key:'aiInfrastructure',group:'AI capabilities & operational authority',label:'Does the solution require infrastructure for AI workloads?',hint:'Identify training, inference, model / data volumes, accelerator needs, storage throughput and capacity utilization. AI can use servers, containers or managed services; a GPU alone does not select a location.',options:[['none','No AI workload'],['training','Model training / fine-tuning'],['inference','Inference / model serving'],['both','Training and inference'],['unknown','AI infrastructure needs not yet established']]},
{key:'embeddedAI',group:'AI capabilities & operational authority',label:'Does the software or platform contain embedded AI capabilities?',hint:'Examples: built-in copilots, automated diagnostics, AI in storage/networking, or vendor telemetry analysis. Consider whether the capability is enabled and whether it calls external models.',options:[['none','No enabled embedded AI capability'],['yes','Embedded AI is enabled or planned'],['unknown','Vendor capability / configuration not confirmed']]},
{key:'aiAuthority',group:'AI capabilities & operational authority',label:'What authority will AI have over infrastructure operations?',hint:'Select the highest intended authority. A0–A2 do not execute production changes. A3 requires approval before execution; A4 requires a predefined, explicitly approved operating boundary. This answer does not authorize AI actions.',options:[['none','No AI used for infrastructure operations'],['A0','A0 Observation — read and interpret authorized information'],['A1','A1 Assistance — diagnostics, correlation and summaries'],['A2','A2 Recommendation — propose actions for human decision'],['A3','A3 Approved Execution — execute specifically approved actions'],['A4','A4 Bounded Autonomy — act within explicitly approved limits'],['unknown','Operational authority not yet defined']]},
{key:'aiData',group:'AI capabilities & operational authority',label:'Where will AI process data, telemetry and operational context?',hint:'Include prompts, logs, configuration, model APIs and support telemetry. External AI processing may conflict with local-execution or sovereignty restrictions even when the main solution runs on-premises.',options:[['none','Not applicable — no AI capability is used'],['local','AI processing remains within institutional premises'],['external','AI uses external models / APIs or transfers context externally'],['unknown','AI data flows or external dependencies not confirmed']]}

];
function aiInScope(r=state.requirements){return r.delivery==='ai'||['training','inference','both'].includes(r.aiInfrastructure)||r.embeddedAI==='yes'||/^A[0-4]$/.test(r.aiAuthority||'');}
function questionApplies(q,r=state.requirements){return q.key!=='aiData'||!aiNotApplicable(r);}
function infrastructureSecurity(r=state.requirements){
 const notes=[];
 if(['internet','mixed'].includes(r.networkExposure))notes.push('Internet exposure: define protected ingress, separate public and administrative paths, authenticate service access, and route relevant security logs to the institutional security function.');
 else if(r.networkExposure==='partners')notes.push('Partner connectivity: restrict approved endpoints and flows, authenticate integrations, and assign responsibility for connection changes and incident coordination.');
 else if(r.networkExposure==='internal')notes.push('Internal access: retain identity-based access and network segmentation; an institutional network is not evidence of trusted users or hosts.');
 if(r.securityIsolation==='segmented')notes.push('Strong logical isolation: validate tenant / workload separation, network policies and administrative boundaries on the indicated platform.');
 if(r.securityIsolation==='dedicated')notes.push('Dedicated physical isolation: verify that the proposed platform actually offers the required dedicated resources. Shared infrastructure is unsuitable unless the requirement is revised through governance.');
 if(r.keyCustody==='institution')notes.push('Institution-controlled keys: validate supported key custody, rotation, revocation and recovery, including what data and administrators the provider can still access.');
 else if(r.keyCustody==='shared')notes.push('Shared key responsibilities: record which party creates, accesses, rotates, revokes and recovers keys; confirm emergency access and service dependencies.');
 else if(r.keyCustody==='provider')notes.push('Provider-managed keys: confirm institutional acceptance, privileged access, jurisdictional exposure and the consequences of losing provider access.');
 if(['isolated','both'].includes(r.trustedRecovery))notes.push('Isolated recovery: design protected / immutable recovery sources, separate administration and dependency independence; validate recovery after production identity compromise.');
 if(['rebuild','both'].includes(r.trustedRecovery))notes.push('Trusted rebuild: define clean configurations, identity restoration, recovery order and validation before reconnection to production.');
 if(r.trustedRecovery==='undefined'||r.trustedRecovery==='unknown')notes.push('Cyber-recovery gap: ordinary backup / DR or an undefined design does not establish trusted recovery. Define the required compromise scenario and end-to-end recovery approach.');
 notes.push('Across all hosting models: define secure configuration baselines, patch and vulnerability-remediation responsibilities, privileged-access controls and authentication, security logging, and incident interfaces with the cybersecurity function. These are architecture requirements, not a cybersecurity certification.');
 if(r.control==='retain')notes.push('Retained privileged operations: preserve institutional authorization and execution boundaries in the hosting and support model.');
 else if(['shared','delegate'].includes(r.control))notes.push('Shared or delegated operations: document privileged provider access, authorization, traceability and institutional oversight of infrastructure changes.');
 return notes;
}
const mandatoryGates=[
 {key:'impact',label:'Service criticality and impact tolerance',hint:'Confirm that the proposed arrangement meets the approved criticality, impact tolerance, RTO (hours) and RPO (minutes). Reference the BIA and architecture evidence.'},
 {key:'connectivity',label:'Connectivity, latency and data gravity',hint:'Confirm end-to-end connectivity, measured latency, bandwidth and data proximity for the proposed arrangement.'},
 {key:'security',label:'Data sensitivity and security controls',hint:'Reference classification, access controls, encryption, segmentation and logging evidence for this arrangement.'},
 {key:'sovereignty',label:'Data and control sovereignty',hint:'Include processing and backup locations, jurisdiction, identity, key custody, privileged support and control-plane authority. Local hosting alone does not establish sovereignty.'},
 {key:'audit',label:'Compliance and auditability',hint:'Reference applicable obligations, audit rights, logging, retention and available assurance evidence.'},
 {key:'resilience',label:'Recovery, dependencies and reversibility',hint:'Confirm end-to-end disaster and trusted recovery, provider concentration, tested recovery evidence and feasible exit. Provider promises alone do not prove recovery.'}
];
const requiredProfileKeys=new Set(['id','name','owner','classification','criticality','financialCriticality','executionRestriction','sovereigntyRestriction','demandProfile','hardwareNeed']);
function requiredMarker(text='Required'){return `<span class="required-marker"><span aria-hidden="true">*</span> ${text}</span>`;}
function profileRequired(key){return requiredProfileKeys.has(key)||(key==='classificationNotes'&&state.application.classification==='custom');}
function requirementLegend(){return `<p class="required-legend">${requiredMarker()} identifies mandatory information. You can continue with “Unknown” / “Not confirmed”, but the requirement remains unresolved.</p>`;}
function field(key,label,obj='application',area=false){let h=obj==='application'?workloadHints[key]:null,id=obj+'-'+key,required=obj==='application'&&profileRequired(key);return `<div class="field"><label for="${id}">${label.replace(/ \*$/,'')} ${required?requiredMarker():''}</label>${h?`<div id="${id}-help" class="field-hint">${esc(h.hint)}</div>`:''}${area?`<textarea id="${id}" ${required?'required aria-required="true"':''} ${h?`aria-describedby="${id}-help"`:''} placeholder="${esc(h?.example||'')}" oninput="state.${obj}.${key}=this.value">${esc(state[obj][key])}</textarea>`:`<input id="${id}" ${required?'required aria-required="true"':''} ${h?`aria-describedby="${id}-help"`:''} placeholder="${esc(h?.example||'')}" value="${esc(state[obj][key])}" oninput="state.${obj}.${key}=this.value">`}${h?`<details class="evidence-help"><summary>Where to get this information</summary><p>${esc(h.source)}</p></details>`:''}</div>`}
function recommendation(r=state.requirements){
 let id=null,reasons=[],issues=[],checks=[],operative=null,support='None proposed',opReasons=[],appliedRules=['C1','C2','I1','V1','V2'],elasticityBased=false;
 const missing=questions.filter(q=>questionApplies(q,r)&&(!r[q.key]||r[q.key]==='unknown')).map(q=>q.label);
 const known=key=>Boolean(r[key]&&r[key]!=='unknown');
 const compatible={saas:'Vendor-hosted SaaS only',package:'Server / VM hosting; confirm supported platform',container:'CaaS on premises or in cloud',modern:'Managed platform or supported self-managed hosting',ai:'Specialized AI infrastructure on premises or in cloud'}[r.delivery]||'Confirm the software delivery model';
 const constraints=[];
 const aiWorkload=r.delivery==='ai'||['training','inference','both'].includes(r.aiInfrastructure);
 if(aiWorkload&&r.aiData==='local'){constraints.push('AI workload processing must remain on institutional premises');appliedRules.push('I4');}
 const a=state.application;
 if(a.executionRestriction==='local')constraints.push('Solution profile requires on-premises execution');
 if(a.sovereigntyRestriction==='local')constraints.push('Solution sovereignty requirement prohibits external hosting');
 if(r.local==='yes')constraints.push('Mandatory institution-controlled execution');
 if(r.cloud==='no')constraints.push('External cloud processing is prohibited');
 if(r.proximity==='hard')constraints.push('Hard local proximity requirement');
 if(r.hardware==='local')constraints.push('Mandatory local dedicated hardware');
 const local=constraints.length>0;
 const requiredPlacement=['delivery','local','cloud','hybrid','proximity','hardware','criticality'];
 if(['package','modern'].includes(r.delivery))requiredPlacement.push('platform');
 const placementMissing=requiredPlacement.filter(key=>!known(key)).map(key=>questions.find(q=>q.key===key).label);
 for(const key of ['financialCriticality','executionRestriction','sovereigntyRestriction'])if(!a[key]||a[key]==='unknown')placementMissing.push(profileOptions[key].label);
 if(aiInScope(r)&&(!r.aiData||r.aiData==='unknown'))placementMissing.push('AI data flows and processing location');
 reasons.push(...constraints.map(reason=>reason+' constrains execution to the local environment.'));
 if(r.delivery==='saas'&&local)issues.push('SaaS-only delivery conflicts with the stated local execution, cloud, proximity or hardware constraint. A supported alternative or an approved change to the requirement is needed.');
 if(r.hybrid==='yes'&&r.cloud==='no')issues.push('Required hybrid composition conflicts with the prohibition on cloud processing.');
 if(r.hybrid==='yes'&&(r.local==='yes'||a.executionRestriction==='local'||a.sovereigntyRestriction==='local'))issues.push('A requirement that the solution execute on institutional premises conflicts with a local/cloud split. Define which components may execute externally before proposing hybrid placement.');
 if(r.delivery==='saas'&&r.hybrid==='yes')issues.push('SaaS-only delivery does not establish a deployable local component. Clarify the solution boundary and assess the components of the hybrid service.');
 if(aiInScope(r)&&r.aiData==='none')issues.push('An AI capability is selected but AI data processing is marked not applicable. Define the processing location and data flows.');
 if(r.delivery==='ai'&&r.aiInfrastructure==='none')issues.push('Specialized AI workload delivery conflicts with the answer that no AI workload is required. Confirm the solution architecture.');
 if(aiInScope(r)&&r.aiData==='external'&&((aiWorkload&&(r.hardware==='local'||r.proximity==='hard'))||r.cloud==='no'||r.local==='yes'||a.executionRestriction==='local'||a.sovereigntyRestriction==='local'))issues.push('External AI models / APIs or telemetry processing conflict with the stated prohibition on external execution or processing. Use an institution-hosted AI capability or disable the external feature.');
 if(placementMissing.length)checks.push('Placement is withheld until these constraints are confirmed: '+placementMissing.join('; '));
 if(!issues.length&&!placementMissing.length){
  if(r.hybrid==='yes'){
   id='HYBRID-COMPOSITION';appliedRules.push('I2');reasons.push('An intentional local/cloud architecture is required and external processing is permitted. Place local-constrained components locally and validate each cloud component separately.');
  }else if(r.delivery==='saas'){
   id='CLOUD-SAAS';appliedRules.push('I2');reasons.push('SaaS-only delivery is compatible with the confirmed permission for external processing, absence of mandatory local execution, flexible proximity and acceptable provider hardware. No local/cloud split is required.');
   checks.push('Validate SaaS lifecycle cost, capacity, service levels and exit before procurement; SaaS compatibility is not a purchase approval.');
  }else{
   let location=null;
   if(local){location='local';appliedRules.push('C1');}
   else if(aiWorkload&&r.aiData==='external'){location='cloud';appliedRules.push('I4');reasons.push('The AI workload explicitly requires external processing, with external execution permitted and no mandatory local constraint. Validate capacity, cost and provider controls.');}
   else if(r.economics==='local'){location='local';appliedRules.push('I5');reasons.push('With no mandatory location constraint, the assessor-supplied economic conclusion favors local execution; supporting comparative evidence requires specialist validation.');if(r.demand==='elastic')checks.push('Elastic demand remains a trade-off: demonstrate local peak capacity and provisioning time despite the local cost advantage.');}
   else if(r.economics==='cloud'){location='cloud';appliedRules.push('I5');reasons.push('External processing is permitted, local constraints are absent and the assessor-supplied economic conclusion favors cloud execution; supporting comparative evidence requires specialist validation.');}
   else if(r.demand==='elastic'){location='cloud';elasticityBased=true;appliedRules.push('I6');reasons.push(elasticityMessage);checks.push('Validate comparable lifecycle costs over a common assessment period, baseline and peak demand, scaling capability and capacity assumptions.');}
   else {appliedRules.push('I7');checks.push('Both local and cloud execution remain possible. Provide comparative lifecycle cost evidence or a decisive capacity requirement; steady demand alone does not choose a location.');}
   if(location){
    if(r.delivery==='container')id=location==='local'?'ONPREM-CAAS':'CLOUD-CAAS';
    else if(r.delivery==='ai')id=location==='local'?'AI-ONPREM':'AI-CLOUD';
    else if(location==='local'){
     if(r.platform==='private')id='ONPREM-PRIVATE-CLOUD';
     else if(r.platform==='self')id='ONPREM-TRAD';
     else checks.push('A local location is indicated, but managed-runtime support does not prove a supported local deployment. Confirm a local platform or self-managed edition.');
    }else{
     if(r.platform==='managed')id='CLOUD-PAAS';
     else if(r.platform==='self')id='CLOUD-IAAS';
     else checks.push('Cloud location is indicated, but only a private-cloud pattern is confirmed. Verify a supported external-cloud hosting pattern before assigning a zone.');
    }
    if(id){appliedRules.push('I3');reasons.push('The software delivery and confirmed platform compatibility select the service model within that location; they do not independently determine the location.');}
   }
  }
 }
 const placementConflicts=[...issues];
 const opInputsKnown=['control','skills','sourcing'].every(known);
 const opConflictStart=issues.length;
 appliedRules.push('I8');
 if(r.delivery==='saas'){
  if(r.control==='retain')issues.push('SaaS provider operation conflicts with required internal execution of privileged / critical solution-stack operations. Clarify whether this requirement only concerns tenant administration.');
  if(r.sourcing==='no')issues.push('SaaS provider operation conflicts with the prohibition on external operational sourcing. Clarify and approve the sourcing boundary.');
  if(issues.length>opConflictStart){placementConflicts.push(...issues.slice(opConflictStart));id=null;}
  else if(opInputsKnown&&id){
   operative='PROVIDER-OPERATED';opReasons.push('The SaaS vendor operates the underlying stack. The stated internal capability and sourcing boundary support a proposed tenant administration / support arrangement, subject to validation.');
   if(['limited','partial'].includes(r.skills))support=r.sourcing==='yes'?'Managed administration / support':'Outtasked specialist administration / support';
  }
 }else if(opInputsKnown){
  if(r.control==='retain'){
   if(r.skills==='strong'){operative='INTERNAL';opReasons.push('Retained critical or privileged execution and declared internal capability suggest internal operation.');}
   else issues.push('Retained internal operations require sufficient internal capability and coverage; address the identified skills gap.');
  }else if(r.skills==='strong'){operative='INTERNAL';opReasons.push('The assessor states that the internal team can operate the defined scope; specialist validation remains required.');}
  else if(r.sourcing==='yes'&&r.skills==='partial'){operative='CO-MANAGED';opReasons.push('Partial internal capability and permitted sourcing suggest an explicit division of operational responsibilities.');}
  else if(r.sourcing==='yes'&&r.skills==='limited'){operative='OUTSOURCED-MSP';opReasons.push('Limited internal capability and permission to delegate suggest managed operations.');}
  else if(['partial','limited'].includes(r.skills)&&r.sourcing==='specialist')issues.push('Specialist support cannot substitute for missing end-to-end internal operating capability. Confirm staffing and coverage.');
  else if(['partial','limited'].includes(r.skills)&&r.sourcing==='no')issues.push('External sourcing is prohibited but internal capacity is insufficient. Build internal operating capability before finalizing the model.');
 }
 const operatingConflicts=issues.slice(opConflictStart);
 if(operatingConflicts.length)operative=null;
 if(!opInputsKnown)opReasons.push('Operating model unresolved: confirm required operational control, internal skills / coverage and sourcing permission.');
 if(operatingConflicts.length)opReasons.push('Operating model unresolved because the stated control, capability and sourcing requirements conflict.');
 if(operative&&!informationProvided(r.operatingEvidence)){operative=null;opReasons=['Operating model unresolved: record the operating scope, skills, staffing, coverage and lifecycle / recovery responsibilities before proposing an arrangement.'];}
 if(!operative)support='Unresolved';
 if(r.recovery!=='yes')checks.push('Document RTO, RPO, trusted recovery, backup independence and dependency recovery order.');
 if(a.financialCriticality==='critical')checks.push('Financial / systemic criticality: validate service impact tolerance and recovery across the full financial-service dependency chain.');
 if(r.criticality==='high')checks.push('Demonstrate critical-service impact tolerance and end-to-end recovery; assess provider concentration and independent trusted recovery.');
 if(id&&['Cloud','Hybrid'].includes(model?.zones.find(z=>z.id===id)?.location))checks.push('Validate approved jurisdictions, data / telemetry flows, key custody, privileged access and provider / subcontractor dependencies.');
 if(['confidential','restricted'].includes(state.application.classification))checks.push('Validate controls for sensitive information: encryption, key custody, privileged access, segregation, logging and permitted data / backup / support locations.');if(['ordinary','sensitive','unknown'].includes(state.application.personal))checks.push('Confirm personal-data handling requirements with the data owner and privacy function.');if(r.delivery==='ai')checks.push('Assess AI data flows, inference location, model / supply-chain dependencies, and A0–A4 authority where AI can affect operations.');
 if(aiInScope(r)){
  checks.push('AI capabilities and data flows — document each AI capability, its data / context flows, external model dependencies and processing locations before approval.');
  if(['training','inference','both'].includes(r.aiInfrastructure)||r.delivery==='ai')checks.push('AI infrastructure — validate training / inference requirements, accelerator capacity, data proximity, throughput, utilization, energy and lifecycle economics.');
  if(r.embeddedAI==='yes')checks.push('Embedded AI — review activation settings, vendor changes, permissions, external calls, disablement and reassessment triggers; platform approval does not authorize every AI feature.');
  if(/^A[0-4]$/.test(r.aiAuthority||'')){
   reasons.push('AI operational authority recorded as '+r.aiAuthority+'. This sets oversight and execution requirements; it does not independently select hosting or authorize actions.');
   checks.push('AI operational authority — validate '+r.aiAuthority+' against least privilege, permitted actions, human oversight, traceable decisions and actions, suspension / rollback, and service criticality.');
   if(['A0','A1','A2'].includes(r.aiAuthority))checks.push('Enforce a no-production-write boundary for '+r.aiAuthority+'; proposed changes remain human decisions.');
   if(r.aiAuthority==='A3')checks.push('A3 — require explicit approval of each executed action through controlled interfaces; AI-generated advice is not authorization.');
   if(r.aiAuthority==='A4')checks.push('A4 — require an explicitly approved permitted-action boundary, enforceable permissions, oversight, auditable actions and effective suspension / rollback. Higher autonomy is not an objective in itself.');
  }
 }
 checks.push(...mandatoryGates.map(g=>'Before institutional approval: '+g.label+'. '+g.hint));
 if(placementConflicts.length)id=null;
 const outstanding=outstandingRequirements(r,placementMissing);
 const economicsBasis=economicBasis(r,elasticityBased);
 const aiStatus=aiNotApplicable(r)?'Not applicable — responses establish that no relevant AI capability is involved':aiInScope(r)?'Relevant AI capability identified; intended authority and controls require specialist validation':'Unresolved — AI applicability has not been established';
 return {id,indicatedId:id,cyberChecks:infrastructureSecurity(r),reasons,issues,placementConflicts,operatingConflicts,checks,missing,placementMissing,compatible,operative,support,opReasons,outstanding,economicsBasis,elasticityBased:elasticityBased&&Boolean(id),aiStatus,intendedAiAuthority:/^A[0-4]$/.test(r.aiAuthority||'')?r.aiAuthority:null,appliedRules:[...new Set(appliedRules)],status:placementConflicts.length?'REQUIREMENTS CONFLICT':!id?'UNRESOLVED':'PLACEMENT PROPOSAL',eligibility:'Unresolved — specialist validation required.',approval:'Pending institutional approval.'};
}
function go(i){hideAcronymTip();if(location.hash.startsWith('#acronym'))history.replaceState(null,'',location.pathname+location.search);step=i;render();window.scrollTo(0,0)}
function answer(key,v){state.requirements[key]=v;if(key==='criticality')state.application.criticality=v;if(key==='demand')state.application.demandProfile=v;if(key==='hardware')state.application.hardwareNeed=v;syncSuggestedNeeds();if(step===1){const aiData=document.getElementById('q-aiData');if(aiData){aiData.required=questionApplies({key:'aiData'});aiData.setAttribute('aria-required',String(aiData.required));}const platform=document.getElementById('q-platform');if(platform){platform.required=['package','modern'].includes(state.requirements.delivery);platform.setAttribute('aria-required',String(platform.required));}hideStatusTip();document.getElementById('live-proposal-content').innerHTML=proposal();enhanceAcronyms(document.getElementById('live-proposal-content'));document.getElementById('progress').textContent=questions.filter(q=>state.requirements[q.key]&&state.requirements[q.key]!=='unknown').length;}else render()}
function render(){hideStatusTip();let names=['Solution profile','Solution Assessment','Recommendation','Framework','Acronyms'];document.getElementById('nav').innerHTML=names.map((n,i)=>`<button class="${step===i?'active':''}" onclick="go(${i})"><span>${i+1}</span>${n}</button>`).join('');document.getElementById('title').textContent=['Describe the solution','Assess the solution','Placement & operating model','Framework & decision rules','Acronyms & definitions'][step];document.getElementById('subtitle').textContent=['Define the software and the institutional service it supports.','Rules suggest a preliminary arrangement; outstanding requirements remain visible.','A reasoned proposal, with evidence and conditions to validate.','Transparent rules within the governed hybrid perimeter.','Plain-language explanations of the terms used in the assessment.'][step];document.getElementById('progress').textContent=questions.filter(q=>state.requirements[q.key]&&state.requirements[q.key]!=='unknown').length;document.querySelector('.counter span').textContent='of '+questions.length+' requirements characterized';document.getElementById('content').innerHTML=(step===1||step===2?'':scopeNotice())+[profile,assessment,result,framework,glossary][step]()+`<div class="foot">Pedro Milagres · Preliminary solution-placement demonstrator<br>Session-only assessment. Entries clear on reload. · <a href="#acronyms" onclick="event.preventDefault();go(4)">List of acronyms</a></div>`;enhanceAcronyms()}
const profileOptions={
 criticality:{...questions.find(q=>q.key==='criticality'),label:'Service criticality'},
 financialCriticality:{label:'Financial / systemic criticality',hint:'Characterize the solution’s role in monetary, payment, settlement or financial-stability services. This strengthens mandatory impact and recovery checks; it is not a universal cloud prohibition.',options:[['critical','Critical financial / systemic service'],['support','Supporting financial or institutional service'],['noncritical','No critical financial / systemic function'],['unknown','Not yet assessed']]},
 executionRestriction:{label:'Mandatory execution location',hint:'Choose on-premises when an institutional requirement prohibits external execution. This directly excludes external cloud, SaaS and hybrid cloud components. Costs cannot override it.',options:[['local','Must remain on-premises — external cloud prohibited'],['flexible','No mandatory local-execution restriction established'],['unknown','Institutional restriction not yet confirmed']]},
 sovereigntyRestriction:{label:'Sovereignty constraint on external hosting',hint:'Consider jurisdiction, identities, encryption keys, privileged access and control-plane authority, not only data residency. A conditional answer still requires supporting sovereignty evidence.',options:[['local','Institutional sovereignty requirement prohibits external hosting'],['conditional','External hosting may be considered if sovereignty controls are evidenced'],['unknown','Sovereignty requirements not yet established']]},

 classification:{label:'Data classification',hint:'Suggested labels only: map these to your institution’s approved policy. Select the highest classification processed by the solution. Sensitivity alone does not require on-premises placement.',options:[['public','Public — approved for public disclosure'],['internal','Internal — routine institutional information'],['confidential','Confidential — disclosure could cause material harm'],['restricted','Restricted / highly sensitive — critical or tightly controlled information'],['custom','Other institutional classification — specify below'],['unknown','Not yet classified — confirm with data owner']]},
 personal:{label:'Personal data',hint:'Personal data is a separate attribute from confidentiality. Confirm with the data owner.',options:[['none','No personal data expected'],['ordinary','Personal data — identifiers, contacts, employee information'],['sensitive','Special-category or highly sensitive personal data'],['unknown','Unknown / requires review']]},
 demandProfile:{label:'Demand & scaling pattern',hint:'This answer also populates the demand question in the solution assessment.',options:[['steady','Predictable / steady capacity'],['elastic','Variable peaks, bursts or rapid scaling'],['unknown','Not yet sized']]},
 users:{label:'Usage / concurrency pattern',hint:'Choose the relevant pattern, then record user counts or rates in the sizing details.',options:[['interactive','Interactive users — specify total and concurrent users'],['transaction','Transactions / APIs — specify requests or transactions per second'],['batch','Batch / scheduled jobs — specify volume and processing window'],['mixed','Mixed users, transactions and batch processing'],['unknown','Not yet established']]},
 compute:{label:'Compute requirements',hint:'Select the main compute characteristic. Add CPU, memory or processing-time estimates if known.',options:[['general','General-purpose CPU / memory'],['cpu','CPU-intensive computation'],['memory','Memory-intensive / in-memory processing'],['gpu','GPU / accelerator-intensive computation'],['appliance','Specialized appliance / dedicated platform'],['unknown','Vendor requirements or sizing not confirmed']]},
 storage:{label:'Storage & data behavior',hint:'Describe initial capacity, growth, retention and I/O or throughput targets in the details.',options:[['standard','Standard solution / database storage'],['iops','High I/O / low-latency transactional storage'],['bulk','Large files, data sets or high-throughput processing'],['archive','Long-term retention / archive'],['mixed','Mixed transactional and bulk / archive data'],['unknown','Not yet established']]},
 hardwareNeed:{label:'Hardware availability constraint',hint:'A GPU or HSM does not automatically require local execution. Choose local only when institutional control or physical proximity makes it mandatory. This updates the hardware assessment question.',options:[['standard','Standard infrastructure or provider-supplied hardware is acceptable'],['local','Local physical / dedicated equipment is mandatory'],['unknown','Hardware constraints not confirmed']]},
 hours:{label:'Service operating window',hint:'Availability hours are separate from recovery targets (RTO / RPO).',options:[['business','Business hours'],['extended','Extended hours / specific processing windows'],['always','24 hours a day, 7 days a week'],['scheduled','Scheduled or occasional execution'],['unknown','Service window not defined']]},
 availability:{label:'Availability requirement',hint:'Choose an architectural requirement; this is not a measured SLA. Record approved numerical targets in the details if available.',options:[['standard','Standard availability; planned downtime acceptable'],['enhanced','Enhanced availability; limited downtime acceptable'],['continuous','Continuous service; redundant design / failover required'],['unknown','Business tolerance not yet agreed']]},
 growth:{label:'Expected growth',hint:'Use an estimate supported by the business. Specify annual percentages or forecast volumes where known.',options:[['stable','Stable / limited growth'],['planned','Predictable planned growth'],['rapid','Rapid growth or uncertain peaks'],['unknown','Forecast not available']]}
};
function optionField(key){const q=profileOptions[key],v=state.application[key]||'';return `<div class="field"><label for="profile-${key}">${q.label} ${profileRequired(key)?requiredMarker():''}</label><div class="field-hint" id="profile-${key}-hint">${q.hint}</div><select id="profile-${key}" ${profileRequired(key)?'required aria-required="true"':''} aria-describedby="profile-${key}-hint" onchange="profileAnswer('${key}',this.value)"><option value="">Select an option…</option>${q.options.map(([id,t])=>`<option value="${id}" ${id===v?'selected':''}>${esc(t)}</option>`).join('')}</select></div>`;}
function profileAnswer(key,value){state.application[key]=value;if(key==='criticality')state.requirements.criticality=value;if(key==='demandProfile')state.requirements.demand=value;if(key==='hardwareNeed')state.requirements.hardware=value;syncSuggestedNeeds();render();}
let needsEdited=false;
function suggestedNeeds(){
 const a=state.application;
 const selected=key=>profileOptions[key].options.find(([id])=>id===a[key])?.[1];
 const lines=['Suggested sizing brief — validate with the solution owner and vendor.'];
 const prompts={
  demandProfile:{steady:'Confirm baseline capacity and peak headroom.',elastic:'Confirm baseline / peak load, peak duration and scaling response time.'},
  users:{interactive:'To confirm: total users and peak concurrent users.',transaction:'To confirm: average / peak requests or transactions per second and response-time target.',batch:'To confirm: jobs, data volume per run and processing deadline.',mixed:'To confirm: concurrent users, transaction rates, batch volumes and processing windows.'},
  compute:{general:'To confirm: vendor-supported vCPU and memory per instance.',cpu:'To confirm: compute benchmark, vCPU and maximum processing time.',memory:'To confirm: active data set, memory per instance and growth headroom.',gpu:'To confirm: supported accelerator model, count, accelerator memory and workload benchmark.',appliance:'To confirm: vendor model, supported configuration and physical requirements.'},
  storage:{standard:'To confirm: initial capacity, IOPS, retention and backup capacity.',iops:'To confirm: peak IOPS, read / write mix, latency and usable capacity.',bulk:'To confirm: initial volume, file sizes, throughput and daily data transfers.',archive:'To confirm: retained volume, retention period and retrieval time.',mixed:'To confirm: transactional, bulk and archive capacity, performance and retention separately.'},
  hardwareNeed:{standard:'Validate hardware and licensing support for the proposed platform.',local:'Confirm required local equipment, location, interfaces and accountable owner.'},
  hours:{business:'To confirm: service hours, time zone and maintenance window.',extended:'To confirm: extended service hours and processing deadlines.',always:'To confirm: support coverage and permitted maintenance arrangements.',scheduled:'To confirm: schedule, job duration and completion deadline.'},
  availability:{standard:'To confirm: agreed uptime target and tolerated downtime.',enhanced:'To confirm: uptime target, redundancy and maximum tolerated interruption.',continuous:'To confirm: uptime target, failover design and recovery validation.'},
  growth:{stable:'To confirm: baseline volume and planning horizon.',planned:'To confirm: annual growth forecast and planning horizon.',rapid:'To confirm: forecast range, peak scenario and capacity review trigger.'}
 };
 for(const key of Object.keys(prompts)){
  const choice=selected(key),prompt=prompts[key][a[key]];
  lines.push(profileOptions[key].label+': '+(prompt?choice+'. '+prompt:'To confirm — '+profileOptions[key].hint));
 }
 lines.push('Supporting evidence: vendor specifications, business volumes and sizing / load-test results — to confirm.','Validation owner and date: to confirm.');
 return lines.join('\n\n');
}
function syncSuggestedNeeds(){if(!needsEdited)state.application.needs=suggestedNeeds();}
function editNeeds(value){state.application.needs=value;needsEdited=true;document.getElementById('needs-mode').textContent='Your edited brief is preserved when profile choices change.';document.getElementById('refresh-needs').hidden=false;}
function refreshNeeds(){if(needsEdited&&!window.confirm('Replace your edited sizing brief with a new suggestion based on the current choices?'))return;needsEdited=false;syncSuggestedNeeds();render();}
function structuredRequirements(){syncSuggestedNeeds();return `<div class="card"><h2>Demand, hardware & target requirements</h2><p>Choose the patterns that describe the solution. The sizing brief below is suggested automatically from your choices.</p><div class="fields">${['demandProfile','users','compute','storage','hardwareNeed','hours','availability','growth'].map(optionField).join('')}</div><div class="field line"><label for="application-needs">Additional information and sizing details for evaluation and reporting</label><div class="field-hint" id="application-needs-help">Review the suggested details and add any information relevant to the evaluation and PDF report. Numerical targets remain “To confirm” until supported by evidence.</div><textarea id="application-needs" class="suggested-needs" aria-describedby="application-needs-help needs-mode" oninput="editNeeds(this.value)">${esc(state.application.needs)}</textarea><p class="meta" id="needs-mode" aria-live="polite">${needsEdited?'Your edited brief is preserved when profile choices change.':'Updates automatically as you select the solution requirements.'}</p><div><button id="refresh-needs" class="secondary" ${needsEdited?'':'hidden'} onclick="refreshNeeds()">Regenerate from current choices</button></div></div><div class="notice line">Demand pattern and hardware availability are reused in the solution assessment. The suggested brief supports requirements gathering; it does not establish sizing or determine placement.</div></div>`;}

function placementProfile(){return `<div class="card"><h2>Criticality & mandatory placement requirements</h2><p>These declarations constrain the preliminary placement proposal and identify requirements for institutional review. They do not validate mandatory eligibility.</p><div class="fields">${['criticality','financialCriticality','executionRestriction','sovereigntyRestriction'].map(optionField).join('')}</div><div class="notice line">${state.application.executionRestriction==='local'||state.application.sovereigntyRestriction==='local'?'External cloud is excluded by the solution profile. On-premises eligibility still requires evidence for security, sovereignty and recovery.':'High criticality strengthens mandatory requirements. An explicit local-execution or sovereignty restriction excludes external cloud; missing requirements leave placement unresolved.'}</div></div>`;}
function profile(){return `${requirementLegend()}<div class="grid"><div><div class="card"><h2>Solution / software identity</h2><p>Assess one solution or end-to-end software service. Describe its required behavior before choosing a zone or provider.</p><div class="fields">${field('id','Solution ID *')}${field('name','Solution / software name *')}${field('owner','Institutional service owner *')}${optionField('classification')}${optionField('personal')}${field('classificationNotes','Institutional label, data types & handling restrictions',undefined,true)}${field('capability','Purpose & required institutional capability',undefined,true)}</div></div>${placementProfile()}${structuredRequirements()}<div class="card"><h2>Service requirements</h2><div class="fields">${field('rto','RTO — time to restore (hours)')}${field('rpo','RPO — acceptable data-loss window (minutes)')}${field('jurisdiction','Jurisdiction, keys & administration')}${field('latency','Latency & data proximity')}${field('dependencies','Dependencies & recovery order',undefined,true)}</div><div class="notice line">Record “To confirm”, the owner and evidence needed when a requirement is unknown. Example text is illustrative; it is not an approved target.</div></div><div class="actions"><button class="primary" onclick="go(1)">Assess this solution</button></div></div><div><div class="card accent"><h2>One solution. Two decisions.</h2><h3>Where should it run?</h3><p>The software architecture and institutional constraints determine the suggested execution location and service model.</p><h3>Who should operate it?</h3><p>Control needs, internal capability and sourcing permission determine a separate operating model.</p><div class="line"><h3>What you need</h3><p class="meta">Software deployment / support documentation; business and data requirements; recovery targets; performance and sizing; internal skills and sourcing policy.</p></div></div><div class="notice">You do not need to score hosting alternatives. Characterize the solution and review the resulting proposal.</div></div></div>`}
function assessment(){let groups=[...new Set(questions.map(q=>q.group))];return `${requirementLegend()}<div class="grid assessment-grid"><div>${groups.map(g=>`<div class="card"><h2>${g}</h2>${questions.filter(q=>q.group===g).map(q=>`<div class="field line"><label for="q-${q.key}">${q.label} ${requiredMarker(q.key==='platform'?'Required for server / managed-runtime software':q.key==='aiData'?'Required when AI is used':'Required')}</label><div class="field-hint" id="hint-${q.key}">${q.hint}</div><select id="q-${q.key}" ${(q.key==='aiData'?questionApplies(q):q.key!=='platform'||['package','modern'].includes(state.requirements.delivery))?'required aria-required="true"':'aria-required="false"'} aria-describedby="hint-${q.key}" onchange="answer('${q.key}',this.value)"><option value="">Select an answer…</option>${q.options.map(([v,t])=>`<option value="${v}" ${state.requirements[q.key]===v?'selected':''}>${esc(t)}</option>`).join('')}</select></div>`).join('')}${g==='Economics & capacity'?evidenceInputs('economics'):g==='Operating capability'?evidenceInputs('operations'):g==='AI capabilities & operational authority'?evidenceInputs('ai'):''}</div>`).join('')}<div class="actions"><button class="primary" onclick="go(2)">View recommendation</button></div></div><div class="live-proposal-column"><section class="card accent live-proposal-panel" aria-labelledby="live-proposal-label"><span class="eyebrow" id="live-proposal-label">LIVE PROPOSAL</span><div id="live-proposal-content" aria-live="polite" aria-atomic="true">${proposal()}</div></section><div class="notice live-proposal-note">Choose “Not confirmed” when evidence is missing. The profile’s mandatory local-execution and sovereignty restrictions exclude external cloud. Criticality and sensitivity determine required assurance. The proposal requires specialist validation and institutional approval.</div></div></div>`}
function proposal(){
 const r=recommendation();
 return `${scopeNotice()}${statusFields(r)}
 <p class="${r.elasticityBased?'economic-qualification':'meta'}">${esc(r.economicsBasis)}</p>
 ${r.intendedAiAuthority?`<p class="notice warning">Intended AI authority: ${esc(r.intendedAiAuthority)}. Recorded intent does not authorize execution. ${r.intendedAiAuthority==='A3'?'Explicit approval is required for each executed action.':r.intendedAiAuthority==='A4'?'An approved permitted-action boundary, least privilege, human oversight, auditability and effective suspension / recovery are required.':'Production changes remain human decisions.'}</p>`:''}
 ${r.issues.length?`<section class="proposal-conflicts" aria-label="Confirmed requirement conflicts"><h3>Confirmed requirement conflicts</h3>${list(r.issues)}<p class="meta">Incompatible arrangements are withheld. Missing information is listed separately below.</p></section>`:''}
 ${outstandingHtml(r)}
 <section class="recommendation-basis"><h3>Recommendation basis</h3>${list(r.reasons.length?r.reasons.filter(x=>x!==r.economicsBasis):['Placement unresolved. Confirm the required inputs and supported architecture.'])}<p class="meta"><strong>Compatible delivery:</strong> ${esc(r.compatible)}</p><p class="meta"><strong>AI applicability:</strong> ${esc(r.aiStatus)}</p><p class="meta"><strong>Applied rules:</strong> ${r.appliedRules.map(esc).join(', ')} · <a href="#framework" onclick="event.preventDefault();go(3)">Recommendation method</a></p></section>
 `;
}
function list(items){return items.length?`<ul class="help-list">${items.map(x=>`<li>${esc(x)}</li>`).join('')}</ul>`:'<p class="meta">No additional item identified from these answers.</p>'}
function result(){let r=recommendation(),z=model.zones.find(z=>z.id===r.id),op=model.operations.find(o=>o.id===r.operative);let gaps=[...r.missing];if(!state.application.classification||state.application.classification==='unknown')gaps.push('Confirm data classification with the institutional data owner');if(state.application.classification==='custom'&&!state.application.classificationNotes)gaps.push('Specify the institutional classification label');['id','name','owner'].forEach(k=>{if(!state.application[k])gaps.push({id:'Solution ID',name:'Solution name',owner:'Institutional service owner'}[k])});return `<div class="actions report-actions"><button id="download-report" class="primary" onclick="downloadReport()">Download PDF report</button><span id="report-status" class="meta" role="status">Includes reasoning, solution answers, evidence gaps and decision notes.</span></div>${typeof aiRecommendationCard==='function'?aiRecommendationCard():''}<div class="grid"><div><div class="card accent"><span class="eyebrow">${esc(state.application.name||'SOLUTION PLACEMENT')}</span>${proposal()}<h3 class="line">Why this operating model?</h3>${list(r.opReasons)}${z?`<h3 class="line">Responsibility boundary</h3><p>${esc(z.responsibility)}</p>`:''}</div><div class="card"><h2>Infrastructure security implications</h2><p>Requirements to validate for the proposed arrangement. No detailed cyber-risk score or compliance conclusion is produced.</p>${list(r.cyberChecks)}</div><div class="card" id="validation-evidence" tabindex="-1"><h2>Evidence & validation before approval</h2>${list([...r.checks,'Verify mandatory security, sovereignty, resilience, connectivity and exit / reversibility controls for the proposed arrangement.','Verify product support, licensing, operational interfaces and responsibility boundaries.','Confirm risk-adjusted lifecycle costs; cost cannot override mandatory controls.'])}</div><div class="card"><h2>Decision record</h2><p>Document the proposal’s rationale, responsible parties and review trigger. Institutional approval remains a separate process.</p><div class="fields">${field('rationale','Rationale / architecture notes','decision',true)}${field('conditions','Conditions & evidence references','decision',true)}${field('owner','Decision owner','decision')}${field('platform','Platform / technology owner','decision')}${field('operator','Technical operator / provider','decision')}${field('authority','Architecture / risk approval authority','decision')}${field('review','Review trigger / date','decision')}</div></div></div><div><div class="card" id="specialist-validation" tabindex="-1"><h2>Specialist validation required</h2><p>Infrastructure specialists, solution owners and relevant subject-matter experts must validate the proposed arrangement, outstanding requirements and supporting evidence. Detailed evidence validation remains outside this questionnaire.</p><p>Use detailed technical, security, sovereignty, resilience and economic assessments proportionate to criticality, complexity and risk. Institutional governance must approve the final decision.</p></div><div class="card"><h3>Institutional accountability</h3><p class="meta">The institution retains service, architecture, security, sovereignty, recovery and assurance accountability under every sourcing model.</p><h3>Model boundary</h3><p class="meta">${esc(methodDescription)}</p></div><button class="secondary" onclick="go(1)">Edit solution assessment</button></div></div>`}
function framework(){return `<div class="card"><h2>Preliminary solution-placement demonstrator</h2><p>${esc(methodDescription)}</p><p>Declared execution restrictions, sovereignty constraints and incompatible requirements are enforced directly. The location, catalog and operating-model mappings are interpretation rules introduced for this tool. No arrangement is automatically marked eligible or approved.</p><p>Applied rule identifiers appear beside each proposal and in the PDF. Recovery, infrastructure security, AI authority and data flows, operating capability and economic evidence remain visible even when a candidate is suggested.</p></div><div class="card"><h2>Recommendation rules and limitations</h2>${traceabilityTable()}</div><div class="grid"><div class="card"><h2>Design principles</h2>${model.requirements.map(r=>`<div class="ref"><strong>${esc(r.principle)}</strong><p>${esc(r.question)}</p></div>`).join('')}</div><div><div class="card accent"><h2>Three related decisions</h2><p>Execution location: where the solution runs.</p><p>Technology / service model: what stack is consumed.</p><p>Operating / sourcing model: who executes operations and support.</p><p>CaaS can run locally or in cloud. Institutional accountability remains internal under every arrangement.</p></div><div class="card"><h3>Validation and limits</h3><p>${esc(elasticityMessage)}</p><p>Economic preferences are assessor-supplied conclusions requiring supporting evidence. The tool does not calculate TCO or establish economic superiority.</p><p>A0–A4 answers record intended authority. A3 and A4 require independently approved controls; questionnaire selection grants no execution authority.</p><p>The demonstrator does not establish real operational effectiveness, regulatory compliance or tested recovery.</p></div></div></div>`;}
fetch('model.json').then(r=>{if(!r.ok)throw Error();return r.json()}).then(d=>{model=d;if(location.hash.startsWith('#acronym'))step=4;render();if(step===4){const target=document.getElementById(location.hash.slice(1));if(target)target.scrollIntoView({block:'start'});}}).catch(()=>document.getElementById('content').innerHTML='<div class="notice warning">The assessment model could not load. Reload to try again.</div>');
